WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.270 line:15%
And today,

2
00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:04.216
we're continuing our time management masterclass

3
00:00:04.216 --> 00:00:07.190
with news you can use.

4
00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:09.600
We've all been worrying more this year.

5
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.670
Oh my God, that's all I do is worry,

6
00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:13.554
stress, worry.

7
00:00:13.554 --> 00:00:14.801
(Drew groaning)

8
00:00:14.801 --> 00:00:17.070
But how do you deal with that?

9
00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.870
I don't want to sit there.
(Drew groaning)

10
00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:22.460
I want, like, actionable help.

11
00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:26.400
And "The New York Times" suggests making time to worry,

12
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.410
to get back to the rest of your day.

13
00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:34.260 line:15%
They say scheduling 15 minutes to freestyle worry

14
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.960 line:15%
and then get over it, rip the anxiety bandaid off.

15
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.310 line:15%
And they also suggest resetting

16
00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:43.618 line:15%
with a special type of breathing.

17
00:00:43.618 --> 00:00:45.710 line:15%
I do agree with that, see,

18
00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:47.130 line:15%
I have breath written on my arm.

19
00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:47.963 line:15%
And guess what?

20
00:00:47.963 --> 00:00:48.929 line:15%
I still forget.

21
00:00:48.929 --> 00:00:51.573 line:15%
You breathe in rocking forward,

22
00:00:51.573 --> 00:00:53.720 line:15%
and you breathe out rocking back.

23
00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:57.813 line:15%
This is me normally.
(Drew groaning)

24
00:00:57.813 --> 00:01:01.125 line:15%
All right, so they call this rock and roll breathing.

25
00:01:01.125 --> 00:01:03.810 line:15%
(Drew groaning)

26
00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:04.830 line:15%
All right.

27
00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:09.540
But, I prefer Van inhaling.
(Drew groaning)

28
00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.120
If,

29
00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.320
if mornings are more of your stumbling block,

30
00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:17.870
then this one really speaks to me, I have to say,

31
00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:22.870
try waking up with the sun, or at least a mini, fake one.

32
00:01:23.267 --> 00:01:26.340
"Yahoo! News" reports people are turning

33
00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:31.340
to sunrise light alarm clocks to help get out of bed easier.

34
00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:35.419
You set when you want the sun to rise,

35
00:01:35.419 --> 00:01:40.122
and then it slowly brightens to wake you up.

36
00:01:40.122 --> 00:01:43.530 line:15%
Or you could just use nature alarms clock,

37
00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:45.073 line:15%
which is my children.

38
00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.282 line:15%
Although my kids are old enough now

39
00:01:48.282 --> 00:01:52.290 line:15%
that they totally sleep in past when we're all supposed to.

40
00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:53.573
That's the irony, parents.

41
00:01:53.573 --> 00:01:57.770
You literally wake up at 4:00 AM, which I've always done

42
00:01:57.770 --> 00:01:59.920
for work anyway, but it never gets any easier.

43
00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:02.380
You get up at 4:00 AM, and then the minute your kids start

44
00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:04.610
to be able to sleep till eight, they got to get up

45
00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:06.070
at six for school.

46
00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:07.013
It is sadistic!

47
00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.340
My child finally wants to be lazy and sleep in,

48
00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.260
and you make me get up and get out.

49
00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:16.523
It's like, you never get off the hamster wheel!

50
00:02:16.523 --> 00:02:20.018
One way some parents approach time management during

51
00:02:20.018 --> 00:02:22.580
at-home learning was a daily schedule,

52
00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:26.697 line:15%
like this color-coded one that went viral on social media.

53
00:02:26.697 --> 00:02:31.697
That is not how it's gone for me and my life.

54
00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:36.360
And I'm just wondering, you color-coded wonder,

55
00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.210
how do you do it?

56
00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:40.980
And Today.com says that tons of other parents

57
00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:43.476
are actually feeling, apparently, the same way I am,

58
00:02:43.476 --> 00:02:46.230 line:15%
and sharing their more realistic schedules,

59
00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:48.490 line:15%
like this one from LawyerKelly.

60
